{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794855279,"nonce":"Lsl0ZUzP+/dLS7RSjKJSJRtPNZE=","title":"The grow overview's history charts are hard to read and hard to trust. They have no axes, no units, no time labels, and no hover feedback — only two faint corner numbers whose meaning is unclear. The shaded Target Band uses one range for the whole Chart window, so daytime readings sit \"out of range\" against night targets and vice versa: the band ignores whether the grow lights are on. One chart (humidity at the 30-day window) renders almost empty due to a band-maths bug, another shows a physically meaningless negative VPD, cards for sensors that aren't bound waste the whole page, and a stray soil-band form floats at the bottom of the grow page looking like leftover debug text.","message":"Charts are rendered by ECharts (SVG renderer) with real axes, units, tick labels, gridlines, and a hover tooltip showing value, time, and unit. The Target Band steps between a day range and a night range following the Light Cycle: Lights-On Periods use the day targets, Lights-Off Periods use new sourced night targets. The app learns light state from the bound light entity's real history when one is bound, otherwise from a per-grow Light Cycle setting (one lights-on time + hours-on per phase, with sourced defaults like 18/6 veg and 12/12 flower — light cycles change per phase). Unbound, dataless cards are hidden; the soil band editor moves into the soil moisture card; the window toggles are renamed 24h/7d/30d; VPD never shows a negative value. All domain logic — light periods, band ranges, presets — stays in Rust; ECharts only draws.\n\n\n1. As a grower, I want every environment chart to have a labelled value axis with units, so that I can read actual measurements without guessing what the corner numbers mean.\n2. As a grower, I want time tick labels and gridlines on every chart, so that I can tell when a change happened.\n3. As a grower, I want a hover tooltip showing value, timestamp, and unit, so that I can inspect any reading precisely.\n4. As a grower, I want the window toggles labelled 24h/7d/30d, so that I know each toggle is a rolling window ending now, not a calendar day.\n5. As a grower, I want the Target Band on temperature, humidity, VPD, and CO₂ charts to step between day and night ranges, so that my day readings aren't judged against night targets.\n6. As a grower, I want the band steps to follow the light entity's real on/off history when one is bound, so that timer overrides and manual light changes are reflected.\n7. As a grower, I want a Light Cycle setting on my grow, so that bands work even without any light entity bound.\n8. As a grower, I want the Light Cycle to change per phase (defaults like 18/6 veg, 12/12 flower), so that historical charts use the schedule in effect at each point in time.\n9. As a grower, I want the Light Cycle defaults to come from cited presets and be user-editable with reset-to-default, so that I can tune them and undo mistakes.\n10. As a grower of autoflowers, I want long-day defaults through flower, so that the schedule matches how autos are actually grown.\n11. As a grower, I want night temperature bands on the environment charts, so that cooler nights are recognised as correct rather than out of range.\n12. As a grower, I want night VPD bands computed with a night leaf offset, so that night VPD isn't overstated by a lights-on assumption.\n13. As a grower, I want CO₂ to show an ambient band during Lights-Off Periods, so that the chart doesn't imply enrichment should run at night.\n14. As a grower, I want the humidity band computed from the actual temperature readings, so that the band sits where the science says instead of in a corner of the chart.\n15. As a grower, I want VPD clamped at zero, so that the chart never shows a physically meaningless negative value.\n16. As a grower, I want charts with no binding and no data hidden entirely, so that the grow overview only shows what my grow actually has.\n17. As a grower, I want the soil band editor inside the soil moisture card, so that it's obvious what it edits.\n18. As a grower, I want headroom padding above the highest point on temperature charts, so that the line isn't smushed against the frame.\n19. As a grower, I want the phase coach to know whether lights are actually on, so that its VPD guidance matches reality.\n20. As a grower, I want the VPD coach tip to stop telling me to \"run higher\" at night, so that the advice matches the science (keep night VPD close to day).\n21. As a grower, I want charts rendered as SVG that follows the app theme, so that they look crisp and native in dark mode.\n22. As a grower, I want binding an on/off entity to the Light role to be clearly offered in the binding UI, so that I can give the app ground-truth light state.\n23. As a screen-reader user, I want chart accessibility labels preserved through the chart migration, so that the app stays usable without vision.\n24. As a developer, I want all band and schedule logic in pure, unit-tested Rust with ECharts as a drawing engine only, so that the science stays testable and the rendering stays polished.\n25. As a developer, I want night presets stored as ranges with source labels (marked unverified where single-sourced), so that the app's numbers stay honest.\n26. As a grower, I want drying and curing charts to keep a single band, so that no meaningless day/night split appears for lights-free phases.\n\n\n- Rendering: ECharts with the SVG renderer forced, bundled at build time via npm + esbuild (tree-shaken), emitted into the frontend's dist. The AGENTS.md architecture line (\"charts as SVG rendered from Rust\") is amended; an ADR records the trade-off. Rust-side glue via js_sys/serde-wasm-bindgen builds the chart option payload — no hand-written application JavaScript.\n- Band model: the band segment structure gains a light-state dimension. The backend resolves, per Chart window, a light-state timeline and emits (phase, lights-on/off) band segments; consecutive segments with identical ranges merge. Band computation stays in the core crate as pure functions.\n- Light-state precedence per window: (1) the bound light entity's real history (the existing on/off staircase data) wherever it has in-window readings; (2) gaps and the whole window when unbound: periods derived from the grow's Light Cycle (lights-on local time + hours-on for the phase in effect, anchored in the grow's canonical timezone via the same phase spans the bands already use); (3) neither: no light state — single band as today.\n- Light Cycle storage: new per-grow fields (lights-on local time; hours-on per phase, nullable → preset defaults). Defaults ship as sourced, phase-keyed presets in core (photoperiod strains: 18 h veg / 12 h flower; autoflowers: long days throughout), user-editable with reset-to-default, per the seed-data discipline.\n- Night presets: added to core as sourced ranges from the research pass — night temperature per phase (seedling 20.0–23.3 °C, veg 18.3–23.9 °C, flower 15.6–23.3 °C), night VPD per phase (germination/seedling 0.5–0.9 kPa marked sources-vary, veg 0.8–1.2 kPa, flower 1.0–1.4 kPa), night CO₂ = ambient 400–450 ppm with enrichment off. Night RH stays derived by the RH-window solver at night temperature with the night leaf offset; the research's fixed RH rows are sanity checks only. Drying/curing keep their existing single bands.\n- Night leaf offset: a separate lights-off constant (−1 °C; sources span 0 to −1) replaces the lights-on −2 °C default in night VPD/RH maths; logged in the decisions doc.\n- VPD clamp: derived VPD clamps at zero in the core derivation, so chart, bands, and any future consumer agree.\n- Humidity band bug: the humidity chart fetches the temperature series and computes the band with the RH-window solver at segment temperature (day offset by day, night offset by night); the current humidity-as-temperature input is fixed at the root.\n- CO₂ day band: sourced from the two enrichment articles already cited in the research during encoding; if no two-source range emerges, ship marked unverified.\n- Coach: the phase coach receives the real light state (sensor if bound, else the Light Cycle) instead of a hardcoded lights-on assumption; the VPD night tip is reworded to \"keep close to daytime; watch the RH spike\" per the research.\n- Card visibility: the grow overview renders a chart card only when its role is bound (or, for pH/EC, when entries exist); the soil band editor renders inside the soil moisture card and keeps its accessible field labels; dead-binding banners still apply when a bound entity goes unavailable.\n- Chart window toggles renamed 24h/7d/30d (rolling windows unchanged); all locale catalogs updated with key parity.\n- SPEC §4.9 is updated to describe the implemented precedence; the phantom preset tables in SPEC §8 are left for separate cleanup.\n\n\n- Good tests assert external behavior — endpoint responses, pure function outputs, the rendered option structure — never internal call graphs.\n- Four seams (confirmed in session):\n  1. Core pure functions: light-period expansion (including DST, following the existing timezone test approach), (phase × light-state) band stepping, night preset coverage, VPD clamp, night offset swap. Prior art: the core band-stepping and preset-coverage test families.\n  2. Backend history endpoint with the mock HA fixture: day/night band segments in the response, Light Cycle field validation, sensor-wins-over-schedule precedence, degraded (snapshot-only) mode still works. Prior art: the existing phase-band history integration tests.\n  3. Frontend option-builder (the one new seam, replacing the old SVG-geometry seam at the same boundary): GrowHistory → ECharts option JSON; assert axes/ticks/tooltip presence, stepped band regions from the segment list, clamped VPD, empty-state handling.\n  4. Playwright e2e: SVG accessibility labels preserved through the migration, renamed toggles, unbound cards hidden, band editor relocation, tooltip presence on hover.\n- Every gate stays green: fmt, clippy native + wasm at deny-warnings, unit/integration tests, WASM build, prose lint.\n\n\n- The harvest forecast Gantt and the feed-fit bar chart (stay hand-rolled).\n- The lamp advisor endpoint's hardcoded dim level (separate ticket).\n- Alert evaluation against night bands (research caveat C3) — future work; noted in the decisions doc.\n- Suspending germination-dome VPD band checks (research caveat C4) — logged as an open item, not built.\n- SPEC §8 phantom preset-table cleanup.\n- Zoom/pan/brush interactions; historical schedule reconstruction from free-text lights log entries; CO₂ enrichment control (service calls remain gated off).\n\n\n- Night-target research with the full source table lives at `.scratch/research/lights-off-targets.md` (scratch, gitignored — copy any source labels needed for preset constants into code/docs).\n- Obligations on implementation: amend the AGENTS.md architecture line; write the ECharts ADR; log in the decisions doc (night leaf offset, coach tip rewording, ECharts build tooling, Light Cycle model, VPD clamp).\n- Existing e2e assertions that count SVG child elements need rework for ECharts' SVG structure; the aria-label contract is retained.\n- The phase enum has a single flower variant, so night flower rows collapse into one band with early/late guidance in prose, mirroring how existing bands collapse sub-rows.\n- Watch the bundle: ECharts must be tree-shaken to the used chart types; the release image must stay free of Node.","files":null}]}